<title>ITALY: Olivetti details restructuring provision.</title>
<headline>Olivetti details restructuring provision.</headline>
<dateline>MILAN 1996-09-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Italian information technology group Olivetti gave a detailed breakdown on Wednesday of a 200 billion lire provision announced in its first-half results.</p>
<p>In a detailed answer to questions put by market regulator Consob, Olivetti said 115 billion lire had been set aside for restructuring, including 44 billion lire for closure of overseas industrial activities, 63 billion for redundancies and downsizing mainly at its Systems and Services company.</p>
<p>Other unspecified provisions included in the 115 billion lire figure accounted for another eight billion lire.</p>
<p>The remaining 85 billion lire in provisions was to account for possible capital losses from divestments. Milan newsroom +392-66102321</p>
